<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN LAST WEEK.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN LAST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse dipped to 5.600 billion litas last week from 5.621</p>
<p>billion litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on</p>
<p>Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					     May 12-16     May 5-10</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		   20,469	  23,276</p>
<p>    Executed orders		    1,692	   1,917</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)		1,464	   1,481</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL	3,723,950     8,807,190</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		  112	     218</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	    4,143,750     6,142,850</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week	53,912,443    60,730,670</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week	20,445,999    4,617,647</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	    3,620,500    3,999,550</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	    3,961,440     6,142,850</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	    5		 14</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	  285,770	 4,807,640</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
